+      "_parts": "maxim_burst fires in three short bursts with silences between (rounds at 0.05 to 0.54, 0.92 to 1.48 and 1.87 to 2.59 s): its part is the last and longest, seven rounds about 120 ms apart, so a cut burst (a Soviet section's 6 or 8, a tank's DT 7, at 10 a second) plays from its first round with no silence in it. Without a part it played whole, 18 rounds for a burst of 6.",
       "endFade": 0.04
     },
+    "tankMg": {
+      "_how": "A tank's machine guns, by army, over mgClose and byNation.mg: a close burst whose shooter is a tank plays her army's row (LandPlay.TankMg names which of her guns fired it, as Noise.Mount); roof is the gun on her commander's hatch, where it differs from her others. Each row is the pack's recordings nearest her guns' rate, measured 22 Nov (each round's time in the take's firing; the median gap between rounds): the pack has no MG 34, M1919, DT or Besa yet.",
+      "GER": ["mg42_burst_01", "mg42_burst_02"],
+      "_GER": "The MG 34 (800 to 900 a minute; LandPlay: 9 rounds at 15 a second): Lubini's two takes whose rounds come 67 and 57 ms apart on average (about 900 and 1,050 a minute), not the three town takes at 49 ms (1,200 a minute, the MG 42's own). The same 7.92 mm round. Her hatch gun is an MG 34 too: this row. mg42_burst_02's firing (0.58 s) is a shade shorter than her burst (0.6 s), so it gives way to 01: in the 1,989-man Normandy recording all 59 close German tank bursts played 01, the same-take rule pitching the copies apart.",
+      "USA": ["tank_mg_burst", "machine_gun"],
+      "_USA": "The coaxial and hull-gunner's M1919 .30 (400 to 600 a minute; 6 rounds at 8 a second): the M240G takes, rounds 92 to 95 ms apart (about 640 a minute), the slowest rifle-calibre gun in the pack. Only the two whose firing outlasts her burst (0.75 s) are on the row: lmg_burst_01 to 03 fire for 0.32, 0.69 and 0.61 s, and a take shorter than a burst plays whole when the give-way picks run out.",
+      "UK": ["tank_mg_burst", "machine_gun", "lmg_burst_02", "lmg_burst_03"],
+      "_UK": "The Besa (450 to 850 a minute; 7 rounds at 13 a second, 0.54 s): the M240G takes, lmg_burst_02 and 03 among them (their firing is longer than her burst).",
+      "SOV": ["maxim_burst"],
+      "_SOV": "The DT (about 600 a minute; 7 rounds at 10 a second): the Maxim, the same 7.62 mm rimmed round, rounds 92 to 137 ms apart (about 500 a minute) in bursts of three to seven.",
+      "*": ["tank_mg_burst", "machine_gun"],
+      "roof": {
+        "USA": ["gunner_burst"],
+        "_USA": "The Sherman's .50 M2 on the commander's hatch (450 to 600 a minute; LandPlay 6 rounds at 8 a second): a real M2 Browning (public domain, approved in the pack as the bomber gunner's), rounds about 120 ms apart (500 a minute)."
+      }
